From 1080552082dff49780852fdc178a6bfd77ae771e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Senior Matthew <SeniorMatt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 02:20:27 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] kcm_plasmakeyboard: sections Feedback/Typing/Alternate
 characters, link to the KWin virtual keyboard page
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Page type: Form (docs/page-design.md 1). Config keys (plasmakeyboardrc General/*), kcfg and the layouts sub-pages are unchanged.

Moved / renamed:
- Top section (no title): 'Keyboard layouts:' button is now 'Choose Layouts…'; new row 'Show on screen:' with a 'Virtual Keyboard…' button
  that opens kcm_virtualkeyboard (KCMLauncher.openSystemSettings), so this page and the KWin page (e75933e) point at each other
  instead of the user guessing which one picks the keyboard and when it appears.
- Checkbox groups get noun section titles instead of 'Key press feedback:'/'General:' form labels: Feedback, Typing, Alternate characters.
  Texts say what happens: 'Play a sound on key press', 'Vibrate on key press', 'Show a popup with the pressed character',
  'Navigate the keyboard with arrow keys', 'Capitalize the first letter of a sentence' (were Sound, Vibration, Character popup,
  Keyboard navigation, Auto-capitalization). Rows kcm_plasmakeyboard/*, relabel: inventory/relabel/kcm_plasmakeyboard.tsv.
- Every control has Accessible.name and KCM.SettingStateBinding (changed-settings highlight; hold delay disabled while the popup is off).
  Handlers use onToggled/onValueModified so loading values never writes them back.
- Markers added on the Add Layout sub-page controls (no wording change) so --strict can prove them.
HIG ids: HIG-001/005/006, HIG-019, HIG-057, HIG-058.

Speed cause (code): none on the main page (plain bindings, no D-Bus or models); the Add Layout page builds the grouped layout models
only when pushed (keyboardlayoutmodel.cpp). Nothing changed there. After-numbers: pending, manager will measure.
Not built yet. Unconfirmed without a build: SettingStateBinding settingName equals the kcfg entry key (soundEnabled etc.; entries have no name=,
so key is the name); handset/mediacenter variants left as they are (Kirigami Addons FormCard, different form factors).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01X5N5x9eWzmrq6QYrYLwQnk
---
 kcm/ui/KeyboardLayoutSelectorListView.qml |   3 +
 kcm/ui/KeyboardLayoutsPage.qml            |   1 +
 kcm/ui/main.qml                           | 111 +++++++++++++++++-----
 3 files changed, 93 insertions(+), 22 deletions(-)

